workedExamples.question_text:
A silo consists of a cylinder of radius $2$ m and height $6$ m, topped by a cone of the same radius and perpendicular height $3$ m. Find its total volume to $1$ decimal place.

The diagram shows an axial cross-section.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1,0)--(1,0)--(1,2.4)--(0,3.8)--(-1,2.4)--cycle;
\draw (-1,2.4)--(1,2.4);
\draw[dashed] (0,2.4)--(0,3.8);
\draw (0,0)--(1,0);
\path (0.5,0) node[below] {$2\text{ m}$};
\path (1,1.2) node[right] {$6\text{ m}$};
\path (0,3.1) node[right] {$3\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A solid consists of a cone of radius $3$ cm and perpendicular height $9$ cm, topped by a hemisphere of the same radius. Find its total volume to $2$ decimal places.

The diagram shows an axial cross-section.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,2.4)--(0,0)--(1.2,2.4);
\draw (1.2,2.4) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.2];
\draw (-1.2,2.4)--(1.2,2.4);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(0,2.4);
\path (0,1.2) node[right] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\path (0.6,2.4) node[above] {$3\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A tank consists of a cylinder of radius $3$ m and height $7$ m, capped by a hemisphere of the same radius. Find its total volume to $1$ decimal place.

The diagram shows an axial cross-section.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,2.6)--(-1.2,0)--(1.2,0)--(1.2,2.6);
\draw (1.2,2.6) arc[start angle=0,end angle=180,radius=1.2];
\draw (-1.2,2.6)--(1.2,2.6);
\draw (0,0)--(1.2,0);
\path (0.6,0) node[below] {$3\text{ m}$};
\path (1.2,1.3) node[right] {$7\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A capsule consists of a cylinder of radius $4$ cm and length $8$ cm with a hemisphere on each end. Find its total volume to $1$ decimal place.

The diagram shows an axial cross-section. The $8$ cm measurement is the length of the cylindrical part.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (0,1)--(3,1);
\draw (0,-1)--(3,-1);
\draw (0,1) arc[start angle=90,end angle=270,radius=1];
\draw (3,-1) arc[start angle=270,end angle=450,radius=1];
\draw[dashed] (0,-1)--(0,1);
\draw[dashed] (3,-1)--(3,1);
\draw (1.5,0)--(1.5,1);
\path (1.5,0.5) node[right] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\draw[<->] (0,-1.5)--(3,-1.5);
\path (1.5,-1.5) node[below] {$8\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Two right square-based pyramids are joined along their matching bases. Each base has side length $4$ cm. Their perpendicular heights are $6$ cm and $9$ cm. Find the total volume.

The diagram shows a vertical cross-section through the apexes and the midpoints of opposite base sides.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0)--(0,1.8)--(1.2,0)--(0,-2.7)--cycle;
\draw (-1.2,0)--(1.2,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,1.8)--(0,-2.7);
\path (0,0.9) node[right] {$6\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,-1.35) node[right] {$9\text{ cm}$};
\draw[<->] (-1.2,2.3)--(1.2,2.3);
\path (0,2.3) node[above] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A monument consists of a square prism with base side length $6$ m and height $4$ m. A right square-based pyramid fits exactly on top. The total height of the monument is $11$ m. Find its total volume.

The diagram shows a vertical cross-section through the pyramid's apex and the midpoints of opposite base sides.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0)--(1.2,0)--(1.2,1.6)--(0,4.4)--(-1.2,1.6)--cycle;
\draw (-1.2,1.6)--(1.2,1.6);
\path (0,0) node[below] {$6\text{ m}$};
\path (-1.2,0.8) node[left] {$4\text{ m}$};
\draw[<->] (1.9,0)--(1.9,4.4);
\path (1.9,2.2) node[right] {$11\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A cone fits exactly inside a cylinder. Both have radius $4$ cm and perpendicular height $15$ cm. What fraction of the cylinder's volume does the cone occupy?

The diagram shows an axial cross-section.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0) rectangle (1.2,3);
\draw (-1.2,0)--(0,3)--(1.2,0);
\draw[dashed] (0,0)--(0,3);
\path (0.6,0) node[below] {$4\text{ cm}$};
\path (1.2,1.5) node[right] {$15\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A hemispherical scoop of radius $5$ cm is removed from a cubic tub of edge length $10$ cm. Its circular opening fits exactly across the top. Find the volume remaining as a percentage of the cube's volume, rounded to the nearest whole percentage.

The diagram shows a vertical cross-section through the scoop's centre.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw (-1.2,0) rectangle (1.2,2.4);
\draw (-1.2,2.4) arc[start angle=180,end angle=360,radius=1.2];
\draw[dashed] (0,2.4)--(1.2,2.4);
\path (0.6,2.4) node[above] {$5\text{ cm}$};
\path (0,0) node[below] {$10\text{ cm}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

